Hmmm... IMO, the thing that makes wizards cool in fiction, and something that
very few rpgs capture, isn't so much the ability to wander around firing force
bolts at everything they meet, but the very occasional and unpredictable bits
of legendary, history changing Big Magic..

So would it be possible to introduce something like this? Probable properties
would be a timeout, a limit on the total number of times you can do it, maybe
the above mentioned requirement for components, and the possibility that it
could go horribly wrong. Possible feats (although these would have to be tuned
to avoid overbalance) would be blapping everything in sight, acting something
like a "oLS,  or creating an artifact from (conferring some selection of
properties on) an object.

Maybe?

